// What the native provider realizes that no census or ledger entry has shown natively (docs/design/graph-integrity.md G9.3, support
// follows capture): by type, its operations, optional members, events and linked relations whose source shape no native check has seen.
// The provider declares them `unverified`: the framework's own surfaces do not offer them until a native check verifies them (a ledger
// entry in docs/coverage/verified.json, or a census), and a mod reads it in a snapshot's `unverified` and an assessment's.
// Generated by `node scripts/coverage.mjs --unverified`; tests/coverage.test.mjs keeps it equal to the ledger. Node built-ins only (none).
